    "description": "For the following areas...\nVolusia-Brevard County Line to Sebastian Inlet 0-20 nm...\nSebastian Inlet to Jupiter Inlet 0-20 nm...\nSebastian Inlet to Jupiter Inlet 20-60 nm...\n\nAt 854 PM EST, a severe thunderstorm capable of producing waterspouts\nwas located over Vero Beach South, moving northeast at 20 knots.\n\nHAZARD...Waterspouts and wind gusts to 40 knots.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Waterspouts can easily overturn boats and create locally\nhazardous seas. Small craft could be damaged in briefly\nhigher winds and suddenly higher waves.\n\nLocations impacted include...\nJaycee Beach, Floralton Beach, Moorings Of Vero Beach, Indian River\nShores, South Beach, Vero Beach, Disneys Vero Beach Resort, Wabasso\nBeach, Gifford, Winter Beach, Florida Ridge, Orchid, Queens Cove,\nVero Beach South, Pepper Beach Park, Wabasso, Indrio, North Beach,\nLakewood Park and Saint Lucie Village.",
