    "headline": "Special Marine Warning issued November 21 at 8:45PM EST until November 21 at 9:45PM EST by NWS Miami FL",
    "description": "SMWMFL\n\nThe National Weather Service in Miami has issued a\n\n* Special Marine Warning for...\nLake Okeechobee...\n\n* Until 945 PM EST.\n\n* At 844 PM EST, severe thunderstorms capable of producing\nwaterspouts were located along a line extending from 9 nm north of\nSand Cut to near Lake Harbor, moving east at 10 knots.\n\nHAZARD...Waterspouts and wind gusts 34 knots or greater.\n\nSOURCE...Radar.\n\nIMPACT...Waterspouts can easily overturn boats and create locally\nhazardous seas. Small craft could be damaged in briefly\nhigher winds and suddenly higher waves.\n\n* Locations impacted include...\nCanal Point, Sand Cut, Pahokee, and Lake Harbor.",
    "instruction": "A Tornado Watch remains in effect until 1000 PM EST for southeastern\nFlorida.\n\nThunderstorms can produce sudden waterspouts. Waterspouts can easily\noverturn boats and create locally hazardous seas. Seek safe harbor\nimmediately.\n\nReport severe weather to the Coast Guard or the National Weather\nService. You can also share your report with NWS Miami on Facebook\nand Twitter.",
