    "headline": "Special Weather Statement issued November 21 at 5:26PM MST by NWS Great Falls MT",
    "description": "Wet road surfaces will quickly become icy with the loss of daytime\nheating. High surface moisture and partial clearing skies will\nlead to increased fog development across portions of Central\nMontana through Sunday morning. Conditions may vary over short\ndistances, with visibility dropping to a quarter of a mile or less\nat times. Also, frost deposition make may some roads slippery,\nespecially bridges and other elevated surfaces.\n\nThose with travel plans should be prepared for sudden changes to\nvisibility and road conditions. Slow down and use your low-beam\nheadlights when traveling and leave extra space between vehicles.",
